{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Managing the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Looking at R\u00e9sum\u00e9s", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express duty, advice, willingness, or intention to do something in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "When + Present Perfect and If", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> and <span class=\"italic\">if</span> to talk about conditions that will be fulfilled before a situation can happen. <br/><br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the Present Perfect to talk about a condition that needs to be completed before another one can occur.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can also use <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with the Present Perfect to suggest that something needs to happen before something else can happen. In that context, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> has the meaning of <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">We'll get started <span class=\"strong\">when </span>everyone <span class=\"strong\">has arrived</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You normally use <span class=\"italic\">if</span> with the Present Simple in an if-clause to talk about a possible outcome. The outcome will be positive if the condition in the if-clause is fulfilled.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">We'll get better reviews <span class=\"strong\">if</span> everyone <span class=\"strong\">works</span> a little harder.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Keep your interactions pleasant even when a customer has been unreasonable and rude. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you are a bartender, server or a cook, you have to be able to accommodate your customer's demands and specifications. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you are easily flustered, you will become overwhelmed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If you don't consistently provide excellent service, you may diminish your restaurant's reputation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When you have finished taking their order, you need to get table two more drinks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You'll need to help up front, when they've left.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Duty or Obligation in the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use a variety of modals to talk about duties and obligations, to express what someone is responsible for and to give strong advice and recommendations. <br/> <br/>You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have to</span> to express duty and obligation in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Let's look at the modals<span class=\"italic\"> must</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">have got to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">should</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You cannot use <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">must</span></span> to express duty or obligation in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should</span> + <span class=\"italic\"> have</span> + past participle to express duty in the past.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You should have told me about your problems with the customers yesterday</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">had to</span> before verbs that talk about necessity. <span class=\"italic\">Had to</span> implies that someone else imposed the necessity on you.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">had to</span> leave the kitchen completely clean before you left</span>. = It implies that it was a duty to leave the kitchen clean, and it may not have been fulfilled.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My former restaurant employees should have been able to handle multiple orders from multiple tables simultaneously, but they couldn't.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They should have memorized the specials.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You should have handled that in a delicate, friendly manner. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We had to provide that service in a friendly manner. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I had to order another round of drinks while grabbing more napkins.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "high-pressure ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "involving a lot of pressure or stress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: Restaurant employees face a high-pressure customer service situation every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about restaurant staff.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "busboy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a young man whose job is to take away dirty dishes from the tables in a restaurant", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The goal of all restaurant employees, from busboy to bartender to manager, is to provide outstanding service and quality food to their customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "specification", "type": "name"}, {"content": "detailed instruction about how something should be made ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You have to be able to accommodate your customer's demands and specifications.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to diminish", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become or make something become smaller or less; to reduce", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you don't consistently provide excellent service, you may diminish your restaurant's reputation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "proliferation ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sudden increase in the amount or number of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There is a proliferation of food allergies and sensitivities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "round of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "drinks for a \u200bgroup of \u200bpeople  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  You may have to order another round of drinks from the bartender, grab more napkins, print a bill and check on table seven's food.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "set", "type": "name"}, {"content": "fixed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even if you have a set schedule, it's possible that it will change.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to call on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask someone to do something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You may be called on to cover a shift on your day off.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob09aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online for information on how to write a r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "With a partner, answer the following questions: What is a r\u00e9sum\u00e9?, What information should be included?, How long should it be?, What are references?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at sample r\u00e9sum\u00e9s online as well.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create your own r\u00e9sum\u00e9 using your personal experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss the features of a r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read samples of r\u00e9sum\u00e9s.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create my own r\u00e9sum\u00e9.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my r\u00e9sum\u00e9 with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Do you like interacting with people? Why or why not? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": 