{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "type": "RSLT", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Working in a restaurant isn't for everyone. Restaurant employees face a high-pressure customer service situation every day. The position needs to be handled in a delicate, tactful manner. If you are going to be a successful restaurant employee, you must possess certain traits.", "id": 1, "time": "1", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The goal of all restaurant employees, from busboy to bartender to manager, is to provide outstanding service and quality food to their customers. When people have chosen to go out to a restaurant for a night off from cooking, or to celebrate a special occasion, the experience is almost as important as the food. As a restaurant employee, it is your job to provide that service in a friendly and professional manner. Keep your interactions pleasant even when a customer has been unreasonable or rude. You represent the restaurant, not just yourself.", "id": 2, "time": "19000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Every customer has different likes and preferences. If you are a bartender, server or a cook, you have to be able to accommodate your customer's demands and specifications. If you don't consistently provide excellent service, you may diminish your restaurant's reputation. There is a proliferation of food allergies and sensitivities and something as innocuous as using the same knife to cut different types of dessert can be a potential health risk. When you have taken steps to prevent health concerns, you reduce the risk of liability for your restaurant.", "id": 3, "time": "56000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Prioritization on the job is a challenge. A good restaurant employee must be able to handle multiple orders from many tables at the same time. You may have to order another round of drinks from the bartender, grab more napkins, print a bill and check on table seven's food. You must be able to handle these tasks with efficiency and poise. If you are easily flustered, you will become overwhelmed.", "id": 4, "time": "95300", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "Restaurant employees need to be prepared to be very flexible with their shifts. Even if you have a set schedule, it's possible that it will change. A big reservation, good or bad weather or a nearby event can mean sudden changes to staffing needs. You may be called on to cover a shift on your day off or you may be be scheduled to work until 9:00 only to find yourself still working at quarter to one.", "id": 5, "time": "122000", "image": "engenn11le05ob09re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le05ob09re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le05ob09re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}